Z||000000||RacinRob||04-30-2001||10:32 AM||||I was wondering if it was normal for the rear calipers to be a *itch to get off.   I made sure the bolts were all the way out... There was a ridge in them but the ridge was no bigger than the ridge on the front rotors.  I don't have the e-brake hooked up either if that helps. To get the rear calipers off I hammered on them with a plastic tipped lead hammer.  <P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||84Bill||04-30-2001||02:03 PM||||Yep they can be a beotch||||reg||1
Z||000002||voyagerspe||04-30-2001||09:25 PM||||calpiers are tough.  Forget the plastic coated hammers, go to the tool box grab your BHF and wack them off. Its not hard at all, ive got 3 fieros and never had a problem getting calipers off and ive never hurt a caliper either.||||reg||7
Z||000003||theogre||04-30-2001||11:38 PM||||There is no reason to beat on the caliper.<P>All you need to do is compress the piston slightly... You'r going to have to do that anyway. Once the arm is off you should be able to get enough with a screw driver to get the caliper off.<P>If the rear caliper is so tight you can't get it off you better make sure the thing isn't dragging the pads.||||reg||1
